irst immunity  challenge you're kind of looking at like  okay  um how are we even going to survive as a  tribe and challenges and so me and romy  were always going to be two that were  like heavily looked at in terms of  private weakness and unfortunately romeo  just had the better connections than me  right  right  well that's interesting because i think  that a lot of people don't see that  there's a lot of complex tribe dynamics  that go into the game it's not just do  you use this advantage or do you vote  for this person and i want to ask when  drea came back from the summit as  viewers we didn't see what her  explanation was for what happened that  day and at least on the episode we  didn't see that she was targeted so what  really happened there and  why didn't she have a target on her  so drea definitely did have a target on  her um  she was one of the most talked about  people for the first few days actually  we climbed up the mountain and then we  climbed back down  and that nothing happened up there and i  was like okay well that's like you know  that seems like a waste of 15 minutes of  screen time honestly if that's true  um so i definitely  um was suspicious of her tori was  targeting draya because trey had thrown  her name out there i was closer with  tori i was happy to vote drayau  roxtroy also had some personality  conflicts with andreas it really seemed  like there were the numbers to getcha  out there and then the real stopping  point unfortunately was romeo because we  didn't realize at the time that um  romeo was so close with tori or not with  tory with drea and thanks to that it  would have been really difficult to uh  to sway gotcha  so do you have any regrets about your  gameplay is there anything that you  would change if you got to do it again  um i mean one of my biggest regrets  honestly is not watching sequester  season three because then i would have  gotten to see tori  and just really throw her under the bus  for that um so that's a